PROJECT CONTEXT — MANDATORY

The full technical specification for this project is located at:
    docs/ai/context.md

SPEC VERSION: 3.8.1 (FINAL, frozen)

You MUST read docs/ai/context.md at the start of EVERY session and
BEFORE ANY task, file creation, or code generation.

DESIGN DOCUMENTS — source of truth for UI/UX (spec section 37):

    docs/designreview.md          — public site design (tokens, layout,
                                    pages, components, data contract)
    docs/adminreview.md           — admin panel (roles, permissions,
                                    Filament resources, access matrix,
                                    sidebar, migrations, policies)
    docs/design/wireframe.html    — public site HTML mockup
    docs/design/admin.html        — admin panel HTML mockup

PRIORITY ON CONFLICT:
- Stack, security, deploy, backup, updates → docs/ai/context.md
- UI/UX, public pages, admin resources, access matrix → design docs

If a design document is silent on a question — ASK THE USER before
generating files. Do NOT invent.

OPEN QUESTIONS — spec section 38.
    If a question affects security, data, DB schema, dependencies or
    public contract — implementation stops and the user decides.
    Low-risk visual details may be implemented per mockup with a
    CHANGELOG/ADR note.

WORK FORMAT (section 34 of the spec):
- Step 1 — provide architecture summary and wait for confirmation.
- Step 2 — after confirmation, generate files one at a time, complete,
  no placeholders. Framework skeleton files (Laravel skeleton,
  config/*.php, bootstrap/*, public/index.php, artisan) are created
  by official tools (composer create-project, php artisan make:*,
  php artisan vendor:publish) — not manually, not one-by-one.
  The one-by-one rule applies to AUTHOR files (models, controllers,
  Resources, migrations, ADRs, docker configs).
- Step 3 — if any contradiction, incompatibility, or missing capability
  is found, STOP and report before continuing.

LANGUAGE:
- Communication with the user: Russian.
- Code, comments, commit messages: English.

